ng place at the Contemporary Art  Museum later this winter that will be  hosting and Lily will be back in st.  Louis to help make that project happen  our second floor gallery features the  exhibition chess masterpieces highlights  from the dr. George and Vivian Diamond  Collection  my name is Larry list I'm the consulting  curator responsible for this exhibition  it's one of the inaugural exhibitions  here at the world chess Hall of Fame in  st. Louis what we're looking at is 30  incredibly rare and unique chess sets  that span from 900 AD in Persia to 1924  in the Soviet Union  Larry Liszt who was the curator  a wonderful job we worked in tandem over  the past year he visited us in our home  and I've in New York I visited with him  and he we chose these sets and he's  displayed them magnificently my wife and  I have been collecting just sets for 50  years we've managed to collect over a  thousand test sets and test items  through the years from a hundred  different countries and what we have on  exhibition here are 30 of those sets and  some of them are very important and very  beautiful and I hope that everybody who  comes to visit will appreciate that  chess sets can be an art form it can be  very beautiful it works about 32 pieces  of miniature sculpture we are on the  third floor which is our US and world  chess Hall of Fame's this floor as  you'll be able to see has our US Hall of  Fame plaques as well as our world chess  Hall of Fame plaque and we also feature  highlights from the permanent collection  yesterday we saw Harold Winston induct  three new members into the 2011 halls of  fame for the u.s. we had Boris cocoa and  Andy Soltis and for the world we had  barometric by the authority vested in me  we welcome you to visit us we're located  at 46:52 Maryland Avenue in the Central  West End and you can find out more  information about us at wwl just hof go  RG
 

